    // for all a,c in 1..4 with b != c and a != b (already ensured in previous state)

    // Wait, the h and v in dp[i-1][a][b][h][v] are for indices 2 to i-2.
    // When we add c at position i, we check if b (at position i-1) is a hump or valley.
    // b is a hump if a < b > c.
