    // State: position i, current value y[i], previous value y[i-1], 
    //        count of humps so far, count of valleys so far.
    // But note: humps and valleys are determined when we have 3 consecutive points.
    // So when we add a new point y[i], we can check if y[i-1] is a hump or valley based on y[i-2], y[i-1], y[i].

