    // i: current index (1-based, from 1 to n)
    // prev: y[i-1]
    // curr: y[i]
    // humps: number of humps identified so far (among indices 2 to i-1, since we need i-1 to be a valid index for hump check, which requires i-2 and i)
    // valleys: number of valleys identified so far

