    // where y[i-1] = a, y[i] = b, 
    // and among the indices 2 to i-1, there are h humps and v valleys.
    // Wait, when we have i >= 3, the index i-1 can be checked. 
    // So after choosing y[i], we can update h and v based on y[i-2], y[i-1], y[i].

    // Let's use:
    // dp[i][prev][curr][h][v] where i is the current position (1..n)
    // prev = y[i-1], curr = y[i]
    // h = number of humps among indices 2..i-1 (these are fully determined)
    // v = number of valleys among indices 2..i-1

