    // i: number of points placed so far (from 1 to n)
    // j: number of peaks formed so far (among positions 2 to i-1, since position i is not yet confirmed)
    // k: number of valleys formed so far
    // prev: y value at position i-1
    // curr: y value at position i

    // When we add a new point with value 'next' at position i+1:
    // We can check if position i (with value curr) is a peak or valley based on prev, curr, next.
    // If prev < curr > next, then curr is a peak -> increment j
    // If prev > curr < next, then curr is a valley -> increment k
    // Also, no segment should be parallel to Ox-axis, so curr != next.

